# etude-5dr.5 implementation

Status: ready for implementation gate.

The change adds top-level manifest-v4 `original_git_sha`, retains caller-stage
post-run `git_sha`, and centralizes the legacy fallback in
`Manifest.OriginalCheckout()`. New v4 records require the run-level value;
versions 0/2/3 retain stage-zero semantics and unchanged serialization.

Every hermetic continuation/re-execution path now uses the immutable run value:
live resume, single-stage replay, forward replay, bench replay, and recorded
replay provenance. Live gate-attempt rewrites also preserve the field.

Regression coverage uses distinct original and caller-post-run commits for:

- a real caller stage commit followed by a failed hermetic stage and resume;
- single-stage replay;
- forward replay;
- replay resolution and recorded replay provenance;
- bench replay;
- v4 schema round-trip and fail-closed missing-field behavior.

Documentation distinguishes run checkout identity from caller-stage output
provenance and records that pre-fix v4 manifests fail closed.

